    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: optional, region-validated owner `postcode`\n\nThe spec: an owner may include a 4-digit `postcode`; when present it must be valid for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode, out-of-range \u2192 400, and it's optional (backward-compatible when absent).\n\n### Files changed\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema with `pattern: \"^[0-9]{4}$\"`. Because it lives on `OwnerFields` (which `Owner` extends via `allOf`), it flows into both the create request and the returned owner. The generated `OwnerFieldsDto` picks up a `@Pattern` constraint, so a malformed value (e.g. `\"12\"`) is rejected as a 400 by Bean Validation.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column + getter/setter (with a matching `@Pattern`).\n\n3. **`model/Region.java`** \u2014 Extended the enum (the codebase's designated single source for region-keyed rules) with each region's inclusive postcode range and an `acceptsPostcode(int)` method.\n\n4. **`rest/advice/InvalidOwnerPostcodeException.java`** (new) + **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 A dedicated exception rendered as a 400 with `errors: [\"postcode\"]`, following the existing one-exception-per-rule idiom and matching the shape of the other owner-creation errors.\n\n5. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `rejectInvalidPostcode(city, postcode)` called from `addOwner`. It's a no-op when the postcode is absent; when present and the city has a known region, it rejects an out-of-range value. Cities with no known region accept any 4-digit postcode.\n\n6. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; updated all four for consistency).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps `postcode` by name in both directions, so it's stored on create and returned on read.\n\n### Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest`: **3/3 pass** \u2014 valid postcode stored & returned, owner without postcode accepted, malformed postcode rejected (400).\n- Full test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
